IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nfp-dates`

-- Family Provision Act 1970 (NT) -- the rules a family member meets in claiming provision out of a dead person's estate:
-- who may apply (s 7), when the Court may order provision (s 8), the time for applying and its extension (s 9), serving
-- the administrator (s 10), provision out of property the deceased appointed by will (s 13), the undertaking where death
-- was presumed (s 14), how an order takes effect (s 16), discharge and variation (s 17), dealing with the provision
-- (s 19), provision out of property already distributed (s 20) and the administrator's protection (s 21).
--
-- SEAT: the family member who claims (spouse or de facto partner, former spouse or de facto partner, child, stepchild,
-- grandchild or parent of the deceased). The Court's judgments ("satisfied", "thinks fit", "in the opinion of the
-- Court", "special circumstances", "proper distribution") are asked as facts and answered conditionally, never decided.
--
-- NEGATIVES (rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05, copied in NOTES.md). JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own
-- words: "is not entitled ... unless" (s 7(2)-(4)), "shall not be regarded as having been maintained ... unless" (s 7(7)),
-- "if the Court is satisfied" (s 8(1)), "where" (s 13(1)), "shall not" (s 17(3), s 20(2)), "is of no force or effect
-- unless" (s 19). NOTHING where it does not: a relationship s 7(1) does not list (the list is not closed with "only"),
-- and powers limited by their own wording (s 17(1) applicants, s 20(1) timing), each with a NOTHING-kind comment.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Family Provision Act 1970 (NT). Copyright in Northern Territory legislation
-- is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Family Provision Act 1970 (NT) -- the rules`

§§ `s 7 -- who is entitled to apply`

-- s 7(1): "each of the following persons is entitled to make application to the Court for provision out of the estate
-- of a deceased person: (a) a spouse or de facto partner ...; (b) a former spouse or de facto partner ...; (c) a child
-- ...; (d) a stepchild ...; (e) a grandchild ...; (f) a parent of the deceased person." "De facto partner", "child",
-- "stepchild" are not defined in this Act (borrowed: the Interpretation Act and the Status of Children Act); they are
-- asked as the relationship. s 7(8): a child born alive after the death is regarded as born before it.
DECLARE `Relationship to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `spouse or de facto partner at the death`
    `former spouse or former de facto partner`
    `child, including one born alive after the death`
    `stepchild`
    `grandchild`
    `parent`
    `another relationship, or none`

-- s 7(7): "a person shall not be regarded as having been maintained by the deceased person immediately before his death
-- unless: (a) there was in force at that time an order of a court requiring the deceased person to pay maintenance to or
-- for the benefit of the other person; (b) the deceased person was, at that time, whether under an agreement in writing
-- or otherwise, maintaining that other person or making a contribution to the maintenance of that other person, being a
-- contribution that, in all of the circumstances, can be regarded as other than a nominal contribution; or (c) a court
-- would, if the deceased person were still living, have power to make an order requiring the deceased person to pay
-- maintenance". A closed definition ("shall not ... unless"): FALSE when no head holds.
GIVEN `a maintenance order was in force against the deceased for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased was maintaining me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased was contributing to my maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that contribution was more than nominal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court would have had power to order the deceased to pay me maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(7) -- I was maintained by the deceased immediately before the death` IF
        `a maintenance order was in force against the deceased for me`
    OR  `the deceased was maintaining me`
    OR  (`the deceased was contributing to my maintenance` AND `that contribution was more than nominal`)
    OR  `a court would have had power to order the deceased to pay me maintenance`

-- The facts s 7 turns on, for one claimant and one deceased.
DECLARE `The claimant` HAS
    `relationship`                                    IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
    `maintained by the deceased`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `my parent who was the deceased's child died before the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent of mine was alive at the death`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `a living parent maintained me before the death`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deceased left a spouse or de facto partner`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deceased left a child`                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 7(1)-(4). (2): a former spouse or de facto partner, or a stepchild, "is not entitled ... unless the person was
-- maintained by the deceased person immediately before his or her death". (3): a grandchild "is not entitled ...
-- unless: (a) the parent of the grandchild who was a child of the deceased person died before the deceased person died;
-- or (b) one or both of the parents of the grandchild was or were alive at the date of the death of the deceased person
-- and the grandchild was not maintained by that parent or by either of those parents immediately before the death". (4):
-- a parent "is not entitled ... unless: (a) the parent was maintained by the deceased person immediately before his
-- death; or (b) the deceased person was not survived by a spouse or de facto partner or any of the children".
-- A relationship s 7(1) does not list: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: the list is not closed with "only"; fork F2).
GIVEN c IS A `The claimant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7 -- I am entitled to apply` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `relationship`
    WHEN `spouse or de facto partner at the death` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `child, including one born alive after the death` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `former spouse or former de facto partner` THEN JUST (c's `maintained by the deceased`)
    WHEN `stepchild` THEN JUST (c's `maintained by the deceased`)
    WHEN `grandchild` THEN
        JUST (    c's `my parent who was the deceased's child died before the deceased`
              OR  (c's `a parent of mine was alive at the death` AND (NOT (c's `a living parent maintained me before the death`))))
    WHEN `parent` THEN
        JUST (    c's `maintained by the deceased`
              OR  (    (NOT (c's `the deceased left a spouse or de facto partner`))
                   AND (NOT (c's `the deceased left a child`))))
    WHEN `another relationship, or none` THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 9 -- the time for applying, and a regulative rule`

-- s 9(1): "an application for an order under section 8 shall be made within a period of 12 months after the date on
-- which administration in respect of the estate of the deceased person has been granted". s 4(1): "administration"
-- means probate or letters of administration "granted in the Territory", and includes an order to collect and
-- administer granted to the Curator of Deceased Estates or the Public Trustee; s 4(2): a grant from outside the Territory
-- sealed by the Court under s 111 of the Administration and Probate Act 1969 is a grant in the Territory "on the date on
-- which it was so sealed".
GIVEN `the grant day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 9(1) -- the last day to apply` `the grant day` MEANS `the day 12 months after` `the grant day`

-- s 9(1) as a duty on the applicant: MUST file the application WITHIN the days from the grant to the last day. s 9(2),
-- (3)(b): the Court "may ... extend the time", "whether or not the time for making an application has expired", so on
-- failure the applicant MAY apply for an extension (the LEST), which s 9(4) shuts once the estate is fully distributed.
-- s 9(5): the application is made "on the day upon which the notice of motion or other document instituting the
-- application is filed". The helper runs the rule over the filing day: a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE matches FULFILLED,
-- and anything else is out of time. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `file the application`
    `apply to the Court to extend the time`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the application must be filed within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST `file the application`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the applicant`
        MAY `apply to the Court to extend the time`

GIVEN `the time of filing` IS A NUMBER
      `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `filing at` `the time of filing` `satisfies` `the rule` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of filing`), (EVENT `the applicant` `file the application` `the time of filing`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Timing` IS ONE OF
    `no administration has been granted in the Territory yet, so the 12 months have not begun (s 9(1))`
    `in time (s 9(1))`
    `in time, within the time the Court extended (s 9(2))`
    `out of time, but I may apply to the Court to extend the time (s 9(2), (3))`
    `out of time, and an extension can no longer be sought: the estate has been lawfully and fully distributed (s 9(4))`

DECLARE `The application` HAS
    `administration granted`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `grant day`                     IS A DATE
    `filing day`                    IS A DATE
    `time extended by the Court`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `extended last day`             IS A DATE
    `estate fully distributed`      IS A BOOLEAN

-- Before any grant, or a filing day before the grant, the 12 months have not begun: the Act is silent on an application
-- made then (NOTHING-kind: silent; reported as its own constructor). Out of time and the estate lawfully and fully
-- distributed: "may not be made" (s 9(4)), a flat negative.
GIVEN a IS AN `The application`
GIVETH A `Timing`
`s 9 -- whether my application is in time` a MEANS
    IF (NOT (a's `administration granted`)) OR (a's `filing day` `falls before` (a's `grant day`))
    THEN `no administration has been granted in the Territory yet, so the 12 months have not begun (s 9(1))`
    ELSE IF `filing at` (`the number of days from` (a's `grant day`) `to` (a's `filing day`)) `satisfies` (`the application must be filed within` (`the number of days from` (a's `grant day`) `to` (`s 9(1) -- the last day to apply` (a's `grant day`))))
         THEN `in time (s 9(1))`
         ELSE IF a's `time extended by the Court` AND (`filing at` (`the number of days from` (a's `grant day`) `to` (a's `filing day`)) `satisfies` (`the application must be filed within` (`the number of days from` (a's `grant day`) `to` (a's `extended last day`))))
              THEN `in time, within the time the Court extended (s 9(2))`
              ELSE IF a's `estate fully distributed`
                   THEN `out of time, and an extension can no longer be sought: the estate has been lawfully and fully distributed (s 9(4))`
                   ELSE `out of time, but I may apply to the Court to extend the time (s 9(2), (3))`

-- Whether the application counts as "made within 12 months after the date on which administration was granted" for
-- s 20(1): filed by the s 9(1) last day. An application in time only by an extension is not (finding 3).
GIVEN `the grant day` IS A DATE, `the filing day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application was made within 12 months after the grant` IF
        (NOT (`the filing day` `falls before` `the grant day`))
    AND (NOT (`the filing day` `falls after` (`s 9(1) -- the last day to apply` `the grant day`)))

§§ `s 8 -- what the Court may order`

-- s 8(1): upon application by a person entitled under s 7, "if the Court is satisfied that adequate provision is not
-- available, under the terms of the will ... or under the law applicable on the death of the person as an intestate ...
-- for the proper maintenance, education and advancement in life of the person ..., the Court may, in its discretion and
-- having regard to all the circumstances of the case, order that such provision as the Court thinks fit be made out of
-- the estate". (2): benefits the deceased conferred by will through a power of appointment count as provision available.
-- (3): "The Court may refuse to make an order in favour of a person whose character is such, or whose conduct is or has
-- been such, as, in the opinion of the Court, disentitles him". s 22(1): the Court "shall ... have regard to the
-- testator's reasons". The Court's satisfaction and opinion are inputs.
DECLARE `Outcome` IS ONE OF
    `not entitled to apply (s 7)`
    `the Act does not list you among those who may apply (s 7(1))`
    `out of time, and the time has not been extended (s 9)`
    `no order: the Court is not satisfied that adequate provision is not available (s 8(1))`
    `the Court may order such provision as it thinks fit, in its discretion (s 8(1))`
    `the Court may refuse an order because of your character or conduct (s 8(3))`

GIVEN `entitled` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `in time or extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied adequate provision is not available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is of the opinion my character or conduct disentitles me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Outcome`
`s 8 -- what the Court may do` `entitled` `in time or extended` `the Court is satisfied adequate provision is not available` `the Court is of the opinion my character or conduct disentitles me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `entitled`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Act does not list you among those who may apply (s 7(1))`
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        IF (NOT e) THEN `not entitled to apply (s 7)`
        ELSE IF (NOT `in time or extended`) THEN `out of time, and the time has not been extended (s 9)`
             ELSE IF (NOT `the Court is satisfied adequate provision is not available`) THEN `no order: the Court is not satisfied that adequate provision is not available (s 8(1))`
                  ELSE IF `the Court is of the opinion my character or conduct disentitles me` THEN `the Court may refuse an order because of your character or conduct (s 8(3))`
                       ELSE `the Court may order such provision as it thinks fit, in its discretion (s 8(1))`

§§ `s 13 -- property the deceased appointed by will`

-- s 13(1): "Where: (a) application is made under section 8 ...; (b) the deceased person has, by his will, exercised a
-- general or a special power of appointment in respect of property, being a power under which the deceased person was,
-- immediately before his death, entitled to appoint the property to himself; and (c) the Court is satisfied that: (i)
-- adequate provision for the person who has made the application cannot justly be made out of other property forming
-- part of the estate ...; or (ii) by reason of the existence of special circumstances, an order should be made ..., the
-- Court may order that provision be made out of, or charged on, the property". (2), (3): property caught by a general
-- devise or bequest under s 35 of the Wills Act 2000 counts as "other property" for (c)(i). A "where" condition: FALSE
-- when it fails (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)).
GIVEN `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased exercised by will a power to appoint the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under that power the deceased could have appointed it to themselves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied other property cannot justly provide for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied special circumstances call for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 13(1) -- the Court may order provision out of the appointed property` IF
        `I have applied`
    AND `the deceased exercised by will a power to appoint the property`
    AND `under that power the deceased could have appointed it to themselves`
    AND (   `the Court is satisfied other property cannot justly provide for me`
         OR `the Court is satisfied special circumstances call for it`)

§§ `s 14 -- where the deceased's death was presumed`

-- s 14: where the grant was made on a presumption of death, the Court "may direct that the provision shall not be made
-- unless the person in whose favour the order is made gives an undertaking or security that he will, if the grant of
-- administration is revoked on the ground that the person was living at the time of the grant: (a) where he has received
-- property other than money under the order, restore the property or, at his option, pay an amount equal to the value of
-- the property at the time he received the property ...; or (b) where he has received money under the order, pay an
-- amount equal to the amount of the money received".
DECLARE `What I must give back` IS ONE OF
    `nothing under section 14`
    `restore the property, or at my option pay its value when I received it, of` HAS `the dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `pay back the money I received, of` HAS `the dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `restore the property or pay its value, and pay back the money, totalling at most` HAS `the dollars` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the Court directed an undertaking or security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grant was revoked because the person was living` IS A BOOLEAN
      `money received under the order` IS A NUMBER
      `value of other property when received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What I must give back`
`s 14 -- what my undertaking requires` `the Court directed an undertaking or security` `the grant was revoked because the person was living` `money received under the order` `value of other property when received` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Court directed an undertaking or security`) OR (NOT `the grant was revoked because the person was living`)
    THEN `nothing under section 14`
    ELSE IF `money received under the order` GREATER THAN 0 AND `value of other property when received` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `restore the property or pay its value, and pay back the money, totalling at most` (`money received under the order` PLUS `value of other property when received`)
         ELSE IF `value of other property when received` GREATER THAN 0
              THEN `restore the property, or at my option pay its value when I received it, of` `value of other property when received`
              ELSE IF `money received under the order` GREATER THAN 0
                   THEN `pay back the money I received, of` `money received under the order`
                   ELSE `nothing under section 14`

§§ `s 16 -- how an order takes effect`

-- s 16(1): "Subject to subsection (2), an order under section 8 operates as if it were a codicil to the will of the
-- deceased person executed by the deceased person immediately before his death." (2): "An order under section 8 in
-- relation to property of a deceased person who died intestate operates as a modification of the provisions of Division
-- 4 of Part III of the Administration and Probate Act 1969 in their application to that property." A partial intestacy:
-- each, in relation to the property it governs (fork F6).
DECLARE `Effect of the order` IS ONE OF
    `as a codicil to the will, made immediately before the death (s 16(1))`
    `as a change to the intestacy rules for that property (s 16(2))`
    `as a codicil for the property the will disposes of, and a change to the intestacy rules for the rest (s 16(1), (2))`

DECLARE `The estate` IS ONE OF
    `a will disposes of the whole estate`
    `there is no will`
    `a will disposes of only part of the estate`

GIVEN e IS A `The estate`
GIVETH AN `Effect of the order`
`s 16 -- how the order takes effect` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `a will disposes of the whole estate` THEN `as a codicil to the will, made immediately before the death (s 16(1))`
    WHEN `there is no will` THEN `as a change to the intestacy rules for that property (s 16(2))`
    WHEN `a will disposes of only part of the estate` THEN `as a codicil for the property the will disposes of, and a change to the intestacy rules for the rest (s 16(1), (2))`

§§ `s 17 -- discharge, variation and suspension of the order`

-- s 17(1): the Court may "upon application made by the administrator ..., or by any person beneficially entitled to, or
-- interested in, a part of the estate ..., discharge, vary or suspend an order made by it under section 8". (2): where
-- the Court has ordered periodical payments or a lump sum to be invested, it "may, if it is satisfied, on an application
-- made by" the same persons, "that the person for whose benefit the order was made has otherwise become possessed of or
-- entitled to means for his proper maintenance, education or advancement in life, discharge, vary or suspend its order or
-- make such other order as is just". (3): "An order shall not be made under subsection (1) increasing a provision made
-- by an order under this Act." (4): notice "shall be served on each person who takes a benefit under the order".
DECLARE `Who applies` IS ONE OF
    `the administrator`
    `a person beneficially entitled to or interested in part of the estate`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Change sought` IS ONE OF
    `discharge, reduce or suspend the order`
    `increase the provision`

DECLARE `Variation answer` IS ONE OF
    `section 17 gives no power on this application: it is not made by the administrator or a person interested in the estate`
    `no: section 17(3) bars an order under section 17(1) increasing the provision`
    `the Court may discharge, vary or suspend the order (s 17(1))`
    `the Court may discharge, vary or suspend the order, or make such other order as is just (s 17(2))`

-- An application by someone else: NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording), reported as its own constructor. An
-- increase sought where s 17(2) applies: s 17(3) bars it only "under subsection (1)", and s 17(2) lets the Court "make
-- such other order as is just" (finding 5, fork F7).
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who applies`
      `change` IS A `Change sought`
      `periodical payments or an invested lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied I have otherwise come to have the means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Variation answer`
`s 17 -- what the Court may do to the order` `who` `change` `periodical payments or an invested lump sum` `the Court is satisfied I have otherwise come to have the means` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN `section 17 gives no power on this application: it is not made by the administrator or a person interested in the estate`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `periodical payments or an invested lump sum` AND `the Court is satisfied I have otherwise come to have the means`
        THEN `the Court may discharge, vary or suspend the order, or make such other order as is just (s 17(2))`
        ELSE CONSIDER `change`
             WHEN `increase the provision` THEN `no: section 17(3) bars an order under section 17(1) increasing the provision`
             WHEN `discharge, reduce or suspend the order` THEN `the Court may discharge, vary or suspend the order (s 17(1))`

§§ `s 20, s 21 -- property already distributed`

-- s 20(1): "Notwithstanding any distribution of the property of the deceased person made by the administrator ... before
-- the administrator had notice of an application for an order under section 8 made within 12 months after the date on
-- which administration was granted, the Court may, subject to subsection (2), order that provision be made under this
-- Act out of any property of the deceased person that has been so distributed." (2): "The Court shall not make an order
-- under subsection (1) if the making of that order would affect or disturb a distribution that was a proper distribution
-- made for the purpose of providing for the maintenance, education or advancement in life of a person who was totally or
-- partially dependent on the deceased person immediately before his death."
DECLARE `Distributed property answer` IS ONE OF
    `the Court may order provision out of the distributed property (s 20(1))`
    `no: the order would disturb a proper distribution for a dependant of the deceased (s 20(2))`
    `section 20 gives no power here: my application was not made within 12 months after the grant`
    `section 20 does not speak to a distribution made after the administrator had notice of my application`

-- Outside s 20(1)'s own terms: NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording), reported as its own constructors (finding 3).
GIVEN `made within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `distributed before the administrator had notice of my application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a proper distribution for a dependant of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Distributed property answer`
`s 20 -- provision out of distributed property` `made within 12 months` `distributed before the administrator had notice of my application` `a proper distribution for a dependant of the deceased` MEANS
    IF (NOT `made within 12 months`)
    THEN `section 20 gives no power here: my application was not made within 12 months after the grant`
    ELSE IF (NOT `distributed before the administrator had notice of my application`)
         THEN `section 20 does not speak to a distribution made after the administrator had notice of my application`
         ELSE IF `a proper distribution for a dependant of the deceased`
              THEN `no: the order would disturb a proper distribution for a dependant of the deceased (s 20(2))`
              ELSE `the Court may order provision out of the distributed property (s 20(1))`

-- s 21: "An action does not lie against the administrator ... by reason of his having distributed the whole or any part
-- of the estate ... if the distribution was a distribution referred to in section 20(2) or if: (a) the distribution was
-- made before the administrator had notice of an application for an order under this Act or notice of an application to
-- extend the time ...; and (b) before making the distribution, the administrator had given notices in accordance with
-- section 96 of the Administration and Probate Act 1969 and the time specified in the notices or in the last of the
-- notices for sending in claims had expired." Where s 21 does not apply, whether an action lies is the general law.
GIVEN `a proper distribution for a dependant of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `distributed before the administrator had notice of my application or extension application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 96 notices were given and the time for claims had expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21 -- no action lies against the administrator for the distribution` IF
        `a proper distribution for a dependant of the deceased`
    OR  (    `distributed before the administrator had notice of my application or extension application`
         AND `section 96 notices were given and the time for claims had expired`)
